1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,880
A bank's favorite number led its workers

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,420
to open 3.5 million

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,250
fake accounts.

4
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,570
It's Wells Fargo,

5
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:07,130
one of the biggest banks in America,

6
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:08,810
and its favorite number is eight.

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:09,800
Why eight? Because,

8
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,310
the boss once wrote to shareholders,

9
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,710
eight rhymed with great.

10
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,490
Every branch got targets,

11
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,270
and every worker got a daily number.

12
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,690
Hit it, and you got a bonus.

13
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,190
Miss it, and you heard about it.

14
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,740
So workers started opening accounts for customers

15
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:22,670
who never asked.

16
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:24,210
They ordered debit cards,

17
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,510
made up PINs,

18
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,230
and even invented email addresses.

19
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:28,430
One card here,

20
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,110
one account there.

21
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:30,090
Every single day.

22
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:31,480
In 2016,

23
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,080
regulators reported two million accounts nobody had

24
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,060
asked for, and 5,300 workers

25
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:36,710
were fired.

26
00:00:37,161 --> 00:00:39,440
Luckily, thousands of customers got brand new

27
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:40,880
credit cards. Unluckily,

28
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,450
some of them also got the fees.

29
00:00:43,009 --> 00:00:43,670
Why did it happen?

30
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,040
Pay a kid for every weed he

31
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,010
pulls, and soon he starts planting weeds.

32
00:00:47,453 --> 00:00:48,710
When the number becomes the goal,

33
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,660
people stop chasing the goal and start

34
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:51,530
chasing the number.

35
00:00:52,005 --> 00:00:53,660
The bank agreed to pay three billion

36
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,620
dollars, and the government banned it from

37
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:56,410
getting any bigger.

38
00:00:56,847 --> 00:00:57,810
So for seven years,

39
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,460
the bank that wanted eight of everything

40
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,630
wasn't allowed to grow.

